  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pilot diaspora angel investors</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This pilot project seeks to unlock diaspora capital for early-stage entrepreneurship in Ghana and Angola by connecting Dutch-based and local angel investors with business supported through the Orange Corners Innovation Fund (OCIF). Through structured matchmaking, investor engagement, and virtual Demo Days, the project will test a mechanism to stimulate diaspora angel investment in African business.This project will build on the work of the Orange Corners programme in Ghana and Angola. Activities will include investment readiness coaching for business, investor onboarding and webinars, virtual Demo Days, legal support for deal structuring, and post-pilot learning documentation.The project strengthens entrepreneurship ecosystems by addressing critical access-to-finance gaps and builds the capacity of business angel networks in both countries. It is aligned with the Dutch development cooperation policy of promoting youth employment and inclusive economic growth. Outcomes include 24 trained investors and business, 2 angel networks strengthened, and up to 4 investment deals facilitated. This pilot will inform the design of a scalable diaspora investment model across Orange Corners countries.</narrative>
  </description>
